## Context
DESIGN.md §4 PR-3 (originally PR-2 and PR-3), honoring R13 and R12.
PR-2 (busy_timeout=5000 on every connection, alone) is CLOSED by the sunset
rule: v1.7.1's `80f8aa0` ships `busy_timeout = 10 s` on every open with WAL
tolerance — overtaken by his own implementation, no PR to send (DECISIONS.md
2026-08-27). The edf2748 evidence (zero busy_timeout anywhere in src/; the
0 ms "database is locked" repro) stands as the record of why it mattered. The
per-page commit-cadence question remains with scoped issue C (0035).
PR-3 stands, verified live at v1.8.0: the build path still reaches
clearStore() (index-manager.ts:462) with no library identity stamped, so a
build for one library wipes another's index — the R12 hazard DESIGN-DELTA
cites. The PR: a build for a different library than stamped refuses with a
notice naming both, instead of clearStore(). The guard, not the multi-library
feature.

## Exit criteria
- [x] PR-2 resolved without a PR: overtaken by upstream `80f8aa0` (v1.7.1, busy_timeout 10 s) — sunset-closed 2026-08-27
- [ ] PR-3: cross-library refusal with both libraries named; clearStore chain as repro
- [ ] PR-3 opened upstream; outcome recorded here

## Amendments (implementation review, 2026-08-26)
PR-2: the persist cadence already exists (index-manager.ts:472-473, 200
items/10 s) BUT crawlOptions overrides it to 500 items/60 s on every fulltext
build (build.ts:321) — the longest-held lock on the path that matters. Per the
re-form that override travels with the cadence question to scoped issue C
(0035); PR-2 stays busy_timeout alone, and its repro is scoped to the
zero-timeout throw the pragma fixes (the fulltext hold window is 0035's
evidence, not this PR's).
PR-3 rescoped: no library identity is persisted today, and build.ts:185-197
deliberately avoids keying by routed library id (users/0 locally aliases
users/<id> on cloud). The PR must (a) stamp a canonical {type,id} with the
personal library normalized to one token, then (b) guard on it — and must not
refuse legitimate rebuilds across the local/cloud seam. Quote his doc-comment
in the body and frame the guard as ENFORCING the documented single-library
assumption (political review, finding 4).
